// CoachCam build configuration (tracked; used by both Debug and Release).
//
// SENTRY_DSN is the address crash and error reports are sent to. It is deliberately EMPTY
// here: with an empty value the app never starts the Sentry SDK and behaves exactly as if
// telemetry did not exist.
//
// The real value lives in an untracked file next to this one:
//     Config/Secrets.local.xcconfig
// Create it with:
//     bash Scripts/set_sentry_dsn.sh "<your DSN>"
// Do not write the DSN in this file, in project.yml or in the Xcode build settings: this
// repository is public, and a value in the build settings would override this file.
//
// xcconfig trap: "//" starts a comment, so a DSN cannot be pasted as-is ("https://..." would
// be cut down to "https:"). The script writes it as  https:/$()/...  which Xcode expands back
// to  https://...  when it fills in the SentryDSN key of Info.plist.

SENTRY_DSN =

// Optional include: silently skipped when the file does not exist.
#include? "Secrets.local.xcconfig"
